    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized intelligence assessment reveals a U.S. military posture characterized by heightened operational tempo and strategic flexibility across multiple theaters, reflecting a deliberate shift toward disaggregated and forward-deployed forces. Carrier strike groups (CSGs) remain the cornerstone of U.S. power projection, with USS Gerald R. Ford (CVN-78) sustaining Mediterranean operations to reinforce NATO commitments, while USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) transitions from the Middle East to the Indian Ocean, and USS George Washington (CVN-73) deploys to the U.S. Central Command area with a cruiser escort. This distribution underscores a strategy to maintain persistent presence in critical regions amid escalating tensions, particularly in the Strait of Hormuz, where Iranian maritime aggression has increased. The deployment of advanced ISR and electronic warfare platforms near the U.S.-Canada border and in the southeastern U.S. suggests enhanced monitoring of northern and coastal airspace, likely in response to evolving threats from state and non-state actors. Strategic airlift operations, including C5M and C560 missions, indicate sustained support for global operations, while bomber and tanker aircraft highlight a readiness posture for long-range strike and deterrence missions. The integration of new technologies, such as combat drones for Marine fireteams and the AIM-242 Malice missile, further demonstrates a focus on extending operational reach and lethality in contested environments. The Arctic domain is also emerging as a key area of interest, with exercises like Northern Viking 2026 signaling growing U.S. and allied attention to the region. Overall, the data points to a military posture that balances deterrence, crisis response, and technological innovation, with a clear emphasis on maintaining advantage in the Indo-Pacific and Middle Eastern theaters.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
